{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "06YV", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : (\\Sh(\\mathcal{C}), \\mathcal{O}) \\to\n(\\Sh(\\mathcal{C}'), \\mathcal{O}')$", "MATH_0002": "$$\nLf^* : D(\\mathcal{O}') \\to D(\\mathcal{O})\n$$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:edbf30cddd996ad8526b41eb110749899609a4e9a9175b79aac125be24b64381", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:82fbc4117e75d77baa8e87488952c1dc8a620c564b2ac57b680838b7cd9509fd", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nLet\n<MATH_0001>\nbe a morphism of ringed topoi. We can use K-flat resolutions to define\na derived pullback functor\n<MATH_0002>\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:06189e444679a62476c9eca8fc99f47c5547d3b5d3357297b7e13f34ed699876", "unit_id": "tag:06YV:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "06YV", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : (\\Sh(\\mathcal{C}'), \\mathcal{O}') \\to (\\Sh(\\mathcal{C}), \\mathcal{O})$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{K}^\\bullet$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0005": "$f^*\\mathcal{K}^\\bullet$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{O}'$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{O}'$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-pullback-K-flat}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:a9e980d71788f341963eed34c295e9812abdb20e0a3e880eda0b640061204340", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:2a4f4cbb3cb924e2c4e51a1677988590e13ff21627f255a47848cc6ab339ffe1", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001>\nbe a morphism of ringed topoi. Let <MATH_0002> be a K-flat complex\nof <MATH_0003>-modules whose terms are flat <MATH_0004>-modules. Then\n<MATH_0005> is a K-flat complex of <MATH_0006>-modules whose\nterms are flat <MATH_0007>-modules.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:432e4173e7ccb7a65afb9b8d1fc959665e336d9663d992380fb469eb8cd1e0aa", "unit_id": "tag:0G7E:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "06YV", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f^*\\mathcal{K}^n$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{O}'$", "MATH_0003": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n\\mathcal{K}_1^\\bullet \\ar[d] \\ar[r] &\n\\mathcal{K}_2^\\bullet \\ar[d] \\ar[r] & \\ldots \\\\\n\\tau_{\\leq 1}\\mathcal{K}^\\bullet \\ar[r] &\n\\tau_{\\leq 2}\\mathcal{K}^\\bullet \\ar[r] & \\ldots\n}\n$$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{K}_n^\\bullet$", "MATH_0005": "$$\n0 \\to \\mathcal{M}^\\bullet \\to\n\\colim \\mathcal{K}_n^\\bullet \\to\n\\mathcal{K}^\\bullet \\to 0\n$$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{M}^\\bullet$", "MATH_0007": "$\\colim \\mathcal{K}_n^\\bullet$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{M}^\\bullet$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{M}^\\bullet$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{M}^\\bullet$", "MATH_0011": "$f^*(\\colim \\mathcal{K}_n^\\bullet) = \\colim f^*\\mathcal{K}_n^\\bullet$", "MATH_0012": "$\\mathcal{O}'$", "MATH_0013": "$$\n0 \\to f^*\\mathcal{M}^\\bullet \\to\nf^*(\\colim \\mathcal{K}_n^\\bullet) \\to\nf^*\\mathcal{K}^\\bullet \\to 0\n$$", "MATH_0014": "$f^*\\mathcal{M}^\\bullet$", "MATH_0015": "$\\mathcal{K}^\\bullet$", "MATH_0016": "$\\tau_{\\leq n}\\mathcal{K}^\\bullet$", "MATH_0017": "$\\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0018": "$\\mathcal{M}_n^\\bullet$", "MATH_0019": "$\\mathcal{K}_n^\\bullet \\to \\tau_{\\leq n}\\mathcal{K}^\\bullet$", "MATH_0020": "$$\n0 \\to \\mathcal{M}_n^\\bullet \\to \\mathcal{K}_n^\\bullet \\to\n\\tau_{\\leq n}\\mathcal{K}^\\bullet \\to 0\n$$", "MATH_0021": "$\\mathcal{M}_n^\\bullet$", "MATH_0022": "$\\mathcal{M} = \\colim \\mathcal{M}_n^\\bullet$", "MATH_0023": "$f^*\\mathcal{M}^\\bullet$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{sites-modules-lemma-pullback-flat}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-resolution-by-direct-sums-extensions-by-zero}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{sites-modules-lemma-j-shriek-flat}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-bounded-flat-K-flat}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{lemma-colimit-K-flat}", "REF_0006": "\\ref{sites-modules-lemma-colimits-flat}", "REF_0007": "\\ref{sites-modules-lemma-flat-ses}", "REF_0008": "\\ref{lemma-K-flat-two-out-of-three-ses}", "REF_0009": "\\ref{sites-modules-lemma-pullback-ses}", "REF_0010": "\\ref{lemma-K-flat-two-out-of-three-ses}", "REF_0011": "\\ref{lemma-K-flat-flat-acyclic}", "REF_0012": "\\ref{sites-modules-lemma-flat-ses}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0002": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:8be4ad55e7d1bba965bebcfcc0ec73cf51bb26b0bffda5d072dc036e6b228818", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:f3d723ceb3a09ead03eef68996bac14dfcb64dd6587135e9c521620246848060", "source_text": "The terms <MATH_0001> are flat <MATH_0002>-modules by\nModules on Sites, Lemma <REF_0001>.\nChoose a diagram\n<MATH_0003>\nas in Lemma <REF_0002>.\nWe will use all of the properties stated in the\nlemma without further mention. Each <MATH_0004> is a bounded\nabove complex of flat modules, see\nModules on Sites, Lemma <REF_0003>.\nConsider the short exact sequence of complexes\n<MATH_0005>\ndefining <MATH_0006>. By Lemmas <REF_0004> and\n<REF_0005> the complex <MATH_0007>\nis K-flat and by Modules on Sites, Lemma <REF_0006>\nit has flat terms. By Modules on Sites, Lemma <REF_0007>\n<MATH_0008> has flat terms, by\nLemma <REF_0008>\n<MATH_0009> is K-flat, and by the long exact\ncohomology sequence <MATH_0010> is acyclic (because\nthe second arrow is a quasi-isomorphism). The pullback\n<MATH_0011>\nis a colimit of bounded below complexes of flat <MATH_0012>-modules\nand hence is K-flat (by the same lemmas as above).\nThe pullback of our short exact sequence\n<MATH_0013>\nis a short exact sequence of complexes by\nModules on Sites, Lemma <REF_0009>.\nHence by Lemma <REF_0010>\nit suffices to show that <MATH_0014>\nis K-flat. This reduces us to the case discussed in the next paragraph.\n\n<STRUCT_0001><STRUCT_0002>\nAssume <MATH_0015> is acyclic as well as K-flat and\nwith flat terms. Then Lemma <REF_0011>\nguarantees that all terms of <MATH_0016>\nare flat <MATH_0017>-modules. We choose a diagram as above and\nwe will use all the properties proven above for this diagram.\nDenote <MATH_0018> the kernel of the map of complexes\n<MATH_0019>\nso that we have short exact sequences of complexes\n<MATH_0020>\nBy Modules on Sites, Lemma <REF_0012>\nwe see that the terms of the complex <MATH_0021> are flat.\nHence we see that <MATH_0022>\nis a filtered colimit of bounded below complexes of flat modules\nin this case. Thus <MATH_0023> is K-flat\n(same argument as above) and we win.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:afde2283de29d557622fd001fb26a6c3f24299f12b704d1862f0490e24898adb", "unit_id": "tag:0G7E:proof"}
